{"archetypes":[{"name":"callsite-audit","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Verify that every invocation of each helper script in SKILL.md and any orchestrating shell properly threads the new --skill flag with no silently-missing propagation paths.","prompt_body":"For every invocation of audit-resolve-prs.sh, audit-map-runs.sh, audit-scan-run.sh, audit-title.sh, audit-preflight.sh, and audit-close-priors.sh that appears in SKILL.md or any orchestrating shell script, confirm that --skill is present and that no call site still hard-codes 'implement' or omits the flag entirely. Also check whether any call site passes an explicit --scans-tsv that would override the per-skill derivation SKILL.md plans to control centrally, and whether run-analysis.sh's --skill is forwarded through all branches in the SKILL.md entrypoint including the --plot-from early-exit path. Flag any invocation line where the flag is absent, positionally wrong, or conflicts with an already-present --log-root or --scans-tsv argument. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"schema-evidence","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Verify that the plan's assumed design-run-log directory contents, TSV column schemas, and JSON field names match actual repo artifacts before the implementer builds against them.","prompt_body":"Read actual larch-logs/design/ run directories to confirm the plan's assumed files (execution-issues.md, execution-issues.ndjson, manifest.json, timing-report.json, run-params.json) exist and carry the field names the plan references (design_classification, larch_version, workflow_path). Check that the scan IDs proposed for scans-design.tsv correspond to scan definitions that already exist in audit-scan-run.sh, and that the TSV column schema (pr_number, run_id, started_at, larch_version, closes_issue) is identical to what scans-implement.tsv currently uses so downstream consumers need no changes. Verify that any downstream script reading the audit-map-runs.sh TSV output handles an empty closes_issue column without crashing or producing wrong output. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"regex-anchor","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Verify the dual-regex backward-compat title patterns for --skill=implement are anchored tightly enough that they cannot accidentally match Design-prefixed report titles, and that implement and design patterns are symmetric where required.","prompt_body":"Inspect the current gh issue list search strings and frontmatter-parse regexes in audit-resolve-prs.sh and audit-close-priors.sh, then check whether the plan's proposed anchors (^\\[(Run Logs Audit |Implement Run Logs Audit )) would match a [Design Run Logs Audit ...] title or vice versa. Verify that the --plot-from legacy-title parser in run-analysis.sh uses an equally tight anchor so a [Design Analysis Report] issue cannot be returned when --skill=implement is passed, and that the plan's stated rejection of legacy [Analysis Report] titles under --skill=design is actually enforced rather than just documented. Check whether audit-preflight.sh's concurrent-audit-window check reuses the same search string as audit-resolve-prs.sh, and flag any divergence that could leave the concurrency guard reading a different title set than the prior-report resolver. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
